# Citation metadata, in the format GitHub and Zenodo both read.
#
# The same claim appears in two places: this file and the footer of the tool
# itself. Two copies of one string is two chances to disagree, so
# scripts/check-citation.mjs asserts this file against the values in
# src/lib/site.ts, which is the source for both.
#
# NO DOI YET. Zenodo mints one when a tagged release is archived there; until
# that happens, the doi field is absent rather than a placeholder, on the same
# reasoning CITATION_DOI in src/lib/site.ts documents: a placeholder that
# looks like an identifier is worse than no identifier, because it can be
# copied into a reference list before anyone checks it. Add the identifiers
# block, matching the reference tool's shape, once a release is archived.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: If you use this software, please cite it as below.
type: software
title: Molarity Converter for Biologics
abstract: >-
  A deterministic browser tool that converts between mass and molar
  concentration for a protein whose molecular weight the user declares,
  along with its source and what that weight is the mass of. No molecular
  weight is supplied, inferred, defaulted or looked up, and no data entered
  by a user leaves the browser.
authors:
  - family-names: Modi
    given-names: A.B.
    affiliation: Ligant AI Incorporated
    orcid: https://orcid.org/0009-0009-3837-6605
# Matches APP_VERSION in src/lib/site.ts and the tag on the archived release.
# The leading v is kept so that this file, the footer and the tag are the
# same string rather than three conventions for one version.
version: v0.1.0
# The day this file was prepared, pending an actual tagged release. Update to
# the day the tag is cut, as the reference tool's own file documents: a
# citation whose release date precedes the released commit points a reader at
# a tree that did not yet exist.
date-released: '2026-09-13'
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: https://github.com/abmodi-ai/Ligant.ai-Molarity-Converter
url: https://benchtools.ligant.ai/molarity-converter/
keywords:
  - molarity
  - mass concentration
  - molar concentration
  - biologics
  - protein
  - antibody
  - reproducible research
